         defines a string literally named app_name, used broadly throughout
         its own UI text, not just its manifest label. Since it has
         per-locale translations of that name and we don't, non-English
         locales fell back to its value ("Launcher:3") instead of ours for
         the app's display label - confirmed on a real published APK via
         `aapt dump badging`. A distinct name avoids the resource-name
         collision entirely rather than fighting it. -->
